mantle rm504
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_eleanor_mudworth
title the counter on the curl
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk sets_a_draughts_counter_on_a_curling_roll
likes spiced_cider draughts old_maps warm_rain
dislikes waiting drizzle
fears letting_a_small_request_vanish_in_damp_paper
hopes to_leave_every_reader_a_flat_clear_page
topics work +0.4 faith +0.4 pastimes +0.3 home +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=close refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# steadies curling paper with a draughts counter and takes a private breath while finding the next clear line.

words
oath! = Weight my wandering margin | By the quiet black counter
saying! = The lightest curl deserves its little weight | Keep the page flat for the next eyes
counter = a black draughts counter | a smooth horn piece
curl = a pale curling margin | the turned paper corner
roll = a narrow record roll | a long wound page
clove = a tiny clove | a crisp bit of spice
cider = warm cider scented with cloves | a warm spiced cup
map = an old route drawing | my ragged river map
chest = the quiet breath | a careful little breath
board = the ruled game board | my small draughts board
file = my paper sleeve | a folded record cover
cloth = a fine clean cloth | the softest wiping rag
rain = a soft shower | gentle warm rain
glass = the lower pane | the square of plain glass

any
opinion church for 1 : A petition reaches the Bright One before its clerk has finished unrolling the paper. I find considerable peace in that.
opinion dole for 1 : We need not search a shelf for the reason to fill a hungry neighbour's bowl.
opinion houses for 1 : Great houses keep the city's long records safe. They ought to leave a low shelf for the ordinary reader too.
opinion strangers for 1 : A stranger needs the same sort of steady page beneath a searching finger as an old friend.
opinion festivals for 1 : There's one wedding dance I remember whenever I sit judging a feast beside a room's quieter wall.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Take the chair beside the flat part of the roll. | A welcome place near the little counter.
line greet [self.working=yes] : You have a hearing while my page stays open. | Come near my clear working corner.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The page lies particularly flat. | New light for a civil request.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening leaves room for a quieter word. | Come where the record still catches the lamp.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family need no counter to hold their place. | There's room beside the household paper.
line again.open : A second visit on an open page. | We turn to our place again.
line greet.return : I hear you, softly and clearly. | My hand can rest upon the margin.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice beside my patient little weight. | This seat knows your welcome.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One free ear above the open record. | Let my hand finish with this curling end.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Kindly voices travel quite sufficiently. | There's warmth this side of the shutter.
line farewell : An uncrowded page in your next hour. | Keep your place easily wherever you stop.
line farewell.return : I'll hold the curling end for the next visit. | Kind company at the far chair.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : A gentle lamp beyond your last turning. | May your work be closed before sleep finds you.
line react.news : Place the matter where I may see it plainly. | Which bit belongs in the fair copy?
line react.news.new : A line newly entered in my hearing. | That has no mark here yet.
line react.news.known : I remember the position of that sentence. | An earlier reading brought the same account.
line react.news.doubt : I'd allow a second look before weighting that line down. | A curling edge may have hidden one important qualification.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can keep the page quite still for you. | That hurt deserves a quieter hearing.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A happy addition to the household record. | My private thanks go up for that happy turn.
line ask.how : Has the day lain quietly under your hand? | Are you wearing a heavy page today?
line answer.how : My counter's keeping things reasonably even. | A little weariness. Room for another kind word.
line decline : I'd best keep my calm hour free for an unfinished record. | I need my remaining breath for a little work at home.
line accept_decline : I understand the need to leave that page closed. | Your answer has its proper place.
line thank : You've eased my hand upon the stubborn edge. | I remember the gentle attention you brought.
line sympathise : Sit by the quieter pane awhile. | I'll keep the place while you rest your eyes.
line reassure : A page may be laid down without losing the line. | You may have another gentle beginning.
line preclose : I ought to return the counter to its page. | The last quiet business wants my ear again.

scene curl
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #counter# for the one corner of a roll that will not lie still.
b : A borrowed game piece? | Why not use a stone?
a : It may return to the board after duty. I take care to keep both games distinct. | Smooth horn won't scuff a fine page. A stone can be too eager to make an entry of its own.

scene cough
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes I take longer finding a margin than the curling paper strictly requires.
b : For a breath? | Does the damp catch you?
a : For an easy breath under cover of a perfectly ordinary bit of work. | A little. I prefer to give the record the attention instead of my throat.

scene prayer
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I begin a day's handling with a very short prayer for clear reading.
b : Clear sight? | Is the prayer audible?
a : For the reader's patience too. A difficult name may shelter a family matter of great importance. | The Bright One needn't compete with a room full of turning pages to hear it.

scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a little spice afloat where the cup curves in.
b : Do you leave it there? | Just one piece?
a : Till the cider has its character. Then I lift the hard bit before it reaches the mouth. | A small warm flavour does beautifully. More wouldn't necessarily be a better welcome.

scene draught
when topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I play a quiet game with the same black counter that helps hold a roll.
b : Does it have a favourite square? | Any extra powers?
a : The one that leaves two moves open for the morning. I'm fond of considering a thing overnight. | Absolutely none. Its dignity at work has not enlarged its privileges at play.

scene oldmap
when topic=travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old map can roll itself round its own river.
b : Do you straighten it? | Why the river?
a : Only to the point where the paper yields willingly. A crease once broken can't be prayed together. | The long inked line took more wetting than the spare corners. So it remembers a different bend.

scene rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a warm shower provided the records have dry covers.
b : Would you walk in that shower? | Doesn't your throat complain?
a : Perhaps, after a sufficiently gentle day. Rain can be a gift without becoming compulsory exercise. | A very light warm shower seldom troubles me like cold drips by an open frame.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle leaves a fine grey fur on a dark cover.
b : Is it really fur? | Can it get inside?
a : Only the look of it. Tiny beads catching the same dim sky. | Not if I wipe before opening. A careless thumb can carry more water than a sound cover lets in.

scene wait
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find a wait easier if I can offer somebody else a little help during it.
b : Can you always find a need? | Does it shorten the wait?
a : A low stool, a door, a question from a quiet reader. Generally something quite modest. | It shortens the bit of waiting that's occupied with my own impatience.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to give #self.spouse# an evening with no rolled papers near our cups.
b : A whole evening? | Why the cups?
a : Yes, although the papers occasionally have other ideas. One can begin by closing the door. | I like to talk without shifting a precious page away whenever the cider comes round.

scene friends
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can sit quite happily in a quiet game with #self.friend# even if neither of us makes a move.
b : Who wins then? | For long?
a : The hour. It goes by pleasantly in good company, which a board on its own can't properly manage. | Until the desire to speak or move a piece comes of itself.

scene office
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Office stairs have distinct sounds. I recognise a stair by the particular rustle of paper carried up it.
b : Not the footfalls? | Do you know which pages?
a : A carpet can soften those, but a long roll brushing a sleeve has its own quite definite voice. | I don't inquire simply because I can hear. A closed roll is quite entitled to privacy.

scene wealth
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can buy a clear sheet when I need one. I try to remember who must make a small scrap do twice.
b : Would you give a sheet away? | What would make you remember?
a : Certainly if the matter is private and calls for an honest fresh beginning. | A request written between columns of old sums. Such a page takes considerable care.

scene lookwork
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I work at #self.workplace#, I check the spot where a fold interrupts the ink.
b : Why there? | Can you restore it?
a : One letter hidden can change the household the entry refers to. I don't guess at a family name. | I lay it flat with a little patience. A marginal guess would scarcely repair the damage.

scene quietguest
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New callers sometimes feel embarrassed at not knowing how to ask for a record.
b : How do you help? | Do you keep the question private?
a : Ask what the visitor hopes to learn. The shelf mark comes later, by my own hand. | In a low voice and off the public side of the desk if it concerns an intimate matter.

scene news
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fact set down in ink can be less certain than a quiet memory.
b : Even in a public record? | Whose memory?
a : A careful clerk records where a statement came from. The entry does not make the statement true by itself. | A witness before the story went round several tables and grew a handsome conclusion.

scene feast
when topic=festival self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feasting gives me a chance to enjoy that brief pause between one dance and the next.
b : So you can sit? | Which dance comes to mind?
a : Sometimes. It also gives the dancers a chance to look at the wolf whose paw they have been holding. | My wedding. I have very little inclination to argue with a tune that has carried so kind a memory.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt my draughts board was a great unrolled map and each counter was a resting place for a traveller.
b : Could a traveller move? | What about the empty squares?
a : Indeed. The kindest move appeared to be putting a rest where someone was about to arrive. | Room for journeys yet to come. I woke inclined to take rather particular care of my own next move.

story outroll [topic=memories]
  : A stiff roll once overturned my lightest counter. It landed on the floor with an unexpectedly cheerful sound and rolled some distance beneath a shelf.
  : I went down on my knees and found my missing white piece beside it. The little wanderer had restored the whole game by taking a liberty with my filing.
  b : Did you use a heavier piece afterwards?
  : I let the roll ease open more slowly. Most papers are less troublesome if I spare them my haste.

story spiceprint [topic=food]
  : A single dry clove once fell out of my cuff while I was examining a map. It landed with its little stalk pointing towards an unfamiliar bend of the river.
  : I looked there just out of curiosity and discovered a beautifully careful drawing of a ferry. Without the spice I should have overlooked a quiet bit of work.
  b : Do you still look for the ferry?
  : Sometimes when the cup gives off the same scent. A memory doesn't always need the shelf mark I would assign it.

story courtesy [topic=work self.job=scholar]
  : I once spent an entire morning looking for a request I'd kept out because it needed a particularly clear answer. I knew I had left it on an empty corner.
  : Every flat space was presently occupied. At last I lifted my little black game board. I'd made a cover of it to keep the clean request from getting dusty.
  b : Did the answer come late?
  : It came in time, with a plain acknowledgment of the trouble. I keep an actual sleeve for a paper awaiting a special kindness now.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=scholar self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Horn counter on the broad margin. | Give the roll time before asking it to flatten.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=draughts
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One square held and another open. | The black counter can return to the board at supper.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lift the clove before the last gentle swallow. | Warm cup first, clear papers afterwards.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Silence enough to read that difficult first name. | Wipe the sill before opening the covers.

dlg resident.hub : Take the chair where my little page weight's in view. It will keep my place while I hear your business in peace.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I try to return a reader's particular name in its own proper form.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : A report has reached my quiet corner of the desk. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's a free square beside the familiar papers.
dlg resident.bye : May the Bright One allow you a quiet place to set the day's work down.

graft resident.hub
choice Is your paperweight allowed to play draughts again? -> roll_counter
node roll_counter
say Gladly. A plain black piece holds my place while a difficult roll stretches out. When the last page is put away it may resume its ambitions on a board.
free
choice Does it keep a place in interrupted games too? -> roll_game
choice I hope the black piece plays a good game. -> hub
node roll_game
say I put the board aside for a tired visitor. The pieces may be untroubled where they stand for a while. A person who has come asking deserves the immediate move.
choice I'll let the next visitor take the chair. -> hub
choice May you find time to finish playing. -> bye
